From: fxtec-pro1x-guix
Subject: [PATCH] Show the shortcuts bar on every layout

The bar was only shown on the terminal layout.  A text field (LibreWolf,
GTK) moves the keyboard to a language layout and hides the bar; terminals
have no text-input here, so going back to foot never selects the terminal
layout again and the bar stays hidden.  Author: wanted all the time
(2026-11-03).
---
--- a/src/pos-input-surface.c
+++ b/src/pos-input-surface.c
@@ -378,13 +378,9 @@
 pos_input_surface_toggle_shortcuts_bar (PosInputSurface *self)
 {
-  GtkWidget *child;
-  gboolean shortcuts_visible = FALSE;
+  gboolean shortcuts_visible;
 
-  child = hdy_deck_get_visible_child (self->deck);
-
-  /* shortcuts bar is only for terminal and when we have shortcuts defined */
-  if (POS_INPUT_SURFACE_IS_TERMINAL_LAYOUT (child))
-    shortcuts_visible = !!pos_shortcuts_bar_get_num_shortcuts (self->shortcuts_bar);
+  /* Pro¹x: on every layout, when we have shortcuts defined */
+  shortcuts_visible = !!pos_shortcuts_bar_get_num_shortcuts (self->shortcuts_bar);
 
   gtk_widget_set_visible (GTK_WIDGET (self->shortcuts_bar), shortcuts_visible);
 }
